## std::net — TcpListener / TcpStream class shells + Shutdown enum.
##
## Wave 2 (#06.8) — class identities + Shutdown enum live here in
## self-hosted Riven source. Methods still flow through the
## static-ctor fast path + runtime_table mangled-name lookup
## (`TcpStream_read` → `riven_tcp_stream_read`, …). A trial
## migration during T#20 attempted to declare these as class-body
## `lib "runtime/tcp.c"` decls with `-> Int` returns (matching the
## void*-boxed Result wire shape), but typeck consults the
## hardcoded method-resolver table in `typeck/method_resolvers/mod.rs`
## that says `bind` → `Result[TcpListener, IoError]`. Declaring
## the lib-decl return type as `Int` caused the user-side
## `match TcpListener.bind(...)` to compile (the user-method
## lookup hit the lib decl first) but produce no output at runtime
## because the Ok/Err arms never matched. The clean fix needs
## either the lib-decl grammar to accept `Result[T, E]` return
## types end-to-end through cranelift's import sig (the void*
## ABI is wire-compatible — only typeck sees the rich form), or
## the lib-decl-vs-typeck-table precedence to flip. Both are
## bigger lifts than the static-ctor carve-out removal; the
## migration is deferred until that lands. Duration / Instant
## (whose `Result`-typed methods are limited) migrated cleanly
## under the same T#20 follow-through; TcpListener / TcpStream /
## File / BufReader stay on the runtime_table path for now.
##
## The Shutdown variant order is the load-bearing contract: tag
## indices must match `RIVEN_SHUTDOWN_{READ,WRITE,BOTH}` in
## library/runtime/net/tcp.c. The `shutdown_tag_stability` pin test
## scans this file instead of stdlib/mod.rs.

class TcpListener
end

class TcpStream
end

enum Shutdown
  Read
  Write
  Both
end
